    {
      "id": "term-eng-t101",
      "termNumber": "101",
      "engSourceId": "eng-t101-v1",
      "title": "possessed",
      "sourceFile": "eng/json/016.content.json",
      "selectedBy": "passage",
      "text": {
        "status": "source",
        "sourceId": "eng-t101-v1",
        "html": "<p>Someone who is <b>possessed</b> by a <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t36-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">demon</data>, which is an <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t47-v1\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">evil spirit</data>, is under the control of this demon. The demon can make the person behave in an unusual or violent way, or it can make the person sick and make him suffer.</p><p>A demon can also give a person special powers, so that person knows things that are hidden for other people. In the cultures surrounding <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t74-v2\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">Israel</data>, sometimes people tried to become possessed by a demon in order to know what would happen in the future, or to receive some secret knowledge. God forbade the <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t259-v2\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">Israelites</data> to do this.</p>",
        "textSha256": "8e1366c97bac80907647cd1275676710ff046c56b4578a8e4ca53f2234d453cf",
        "provenance": {
          "status": "source",
